---A device owned by an enterprise. Unless otherwise noted, all fields are read-only and can't be modified by enterprises.devices.patch.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.Device
---@field name? string The name of the device in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/devices/{deviceId}.
---@field softwareInfo? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.SoftwareInfo Detailed information about the device software. This information is only available if softwareInfoEnabled is true in the device's policy.
---@field enrollmentTime? string The time of device enrollment.
---@field networkInfo? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.NetworkInfo Device network information. This information is only available if networkInfoEnabled is true in the device's policy.
---@field lastPolicyComplianceReportTime? string Deprecated.
---@field appliedPasswordPolicies? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PasswordRequirementsList The password requirements currently applied to the device. This field exists because the applied requirements may be slightly different from those specified in passwordPolicies in some cases. Note that this field does not provide information about password compliance. For non-compliance information, see nonComplianceDetails. NonComplianceDetail.fieldPath, is set based on passwordPolicies, not based on this field.
---@field enrollmentTokenName? string If the device was enrolled with an enrollment token, this field contains the name of the token.
---@field hardwareStatusSamples? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.HardwareStatusList Hardware status samples in chronological order. This information is only available if hardwareStatusEnabled is true in the device's policy.
---@field user? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.User The user who owns the device.
---@field applicationReports? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.ApplicationReportList Reports for apps installed on the device. This information is only available when application_reports_enabled is true in the device's policy.
---@field defaultApplicationInfo? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DefaultApplicationInfoList Output only. The default application information for the DefaultApplicationType. This information is only available if defaultApplicationInfoReportingEnabled is true in the device's policy. Available on Android 16 and above.All app types are reported on fully managed devices. DEFAULT_BROWSER, DEFAULT_CALL_REDIRECTION, DEFAULT_CALL_SCREENING and DEFAULT_DIALER types are reported for the work profiles on company-owned devices with a work profile and personally-owned devices. DEFAULT_WALLET is also reported for company-owned devices with a work profile, but will only include work profile information.
---@field enrollmentTokenData? string If the device was enrolled with an enrollment token with additional data provided, this field contains that data.
---@field ownership? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceOwnershipEnum Ownership of the managed device.
---@field lastPolicySyncTime? string The last time the device fetched its policy.
---@field appliedPolicyVersion? string The version of the policy currently applied to the device.
---@field memoryEvents? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.MemoryEventList Events related to memory and storage measurements in chronological order. This information is only available if memoryInfoEnabled is true in the device's policy.Events are retained for a certain period of time and old events are deleted.
---@field lastStatusReportTime? string The last time the device sent a status report.
---@field powerManagementEvents? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PowerManagementEventList Power management events on the device in chronological order. This information is only available if powerManagementEventsEnabled is true in the device's policy.
---@field dpcMigrationInfo? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DpcMigrationInfo Output only. Information related to whether this device was migrated from being managed by another Device Policy Controller (DPC).
---@field disabledReason? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.UserFacingMessage If the device state is DISABLED, an optional message that is displayed on the device indicating the reason the device is disabled. This field can be modified by a patch request.
---@field apiLevel? number The API level of the Android platform version running on the device.
---@field policyCompliant? boolean Whether the device is compliant with its policy.
---@field systemProperties? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.StringMap Map of selected system properties name and value related to the device. This information is only available if systemPropertiesEnabled is true in the device's policy.
---@field commonCriteriaModeInfo? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.CommonCriteriaModeInfo Information about Common Criteria Mode—security standards defined in the Common Criteria for Information Technology Security Evaluation (https://www.commoncriteriaportal.org/) (CC).This information is only available if statusReportingSettings.commonCriteriaModeEnabled is true in the device's policy the device is company-owned.
---@field appliedPolicyName? string The name of the policy currently applied to the device.
---@field nonComplianceDetails? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.NonComplianceDetailList Details about policy settings that the device is not compliant with.
---@field previousDeviceNames? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.StringList If the same physical device has been enrolled multiple times, this field contains its previous device names. The serial number is used as the unique identifier to determine if the same physical device has enrolled previously. The names are in chronological order.
---@field memoryInfo? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.MemoryInfo Memory information: contains information about device memory and storage.
---@field displays? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DisplayList Detailed information about displays on the device. This information is only available if displayInfoEnabled is true in the device's policy.
---@field deviceSettings? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceSettings Device settings information. This information is only available if deviceSettingsEnabled is true in the device's policy.
---@field state? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceStateEnum The state to be applied to the device. This field can be modified by a patch request. Note that when calling enterprises.devices.patch, ACTIVE and DISABLED are the only allowable values. To enter the device into a DELETED state, call enterprises.devices.delete.
---@field appliedState? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceAppliedStateEnum The state currently applied to the device.
---@field userName? string The resource name of the user that owns this device in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/users/{userId}.
---@field hardwareInfo? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.HardwareInfo Detailed information about the device hardware.
---@field managementMode? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceManagementModeEnum The type of management mode Android Device Policy takes on the device. This influences which policy settings are supported.
---@field securityPosture? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.SecurityPosture Device's security posture value that reflects how secure the device is.
---@field policyName? string The name of the policy applied to the device, in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/policies/{policyId}. If not specified, the policy_name for the device's user is applied. This field can be modified by a patch request. You can specify only the policyId when calling enterprises.devices.patch, as long as the policyId doesn’t contain any slashes. The rest of the policy name is inferred.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceAppliedStateEnum "DEVICE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ACTIVE"|"DISABLED"|"DELETED"|"PROVISIONING"|"LOST"|"PREPARING_FOR_MIGRATION"|"DEACTIVATED_BY_DEVICE_FINANCE"

---Covers controls for device connectivity such as Wi-Fi, USB data access, keyboard/mouse connections, and more.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceConnectivityManagement
---@field bluetoothSharing? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceConnectivityManagementBluetoothSharingEnum|string Optional. Controls whether Bluetooth sharing is allowed.
---@field privateDnsSettings? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PrivateDnsSettings Optional. The global private DNS settings.
---@field preferentialNetworkServiceSettings? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceSettings Optional. Preferential network service configuration. Setting this field will override preferentialNetworkService. This can be set on both work profiles and fully managed devices on Android 13 and above. See 5G network slicing (https://developers.google.com/android/management/5g-network-slicing) guide for more details.
---@field tetheringSettings? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DeviceConnectivityManagementTetheringSettingsEnum|string Optional. Controls tethering settings. Based on the value set, the user is partially or fully disallowed from using different forms of tethering.
