---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.EuiccChipInfoList gcp.androidmanagement_v1.EuiccChipInfo[]

---Configuration to enable an app as an extension app, with the capability of interacting with Android Device Policy offline. For Android versions 11 and above, extension apps are exempt from battery restrictions so will not be placed into the restricted App Standby Bucket (https://developer.android.com/topic/performance/appstandby#restricted-bucket). Extensions apps are also protected against users clearing their data or force-closing the application, although admins can continue to use the clear app data command on extension apps if needed for Android 11 and above.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.ExtensionConfig
---@field signingKeyFingerprintsSha256? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.StringList Hex-encoded SHA-256 hashes of the signing key certificates of the extension app. Only hexadecimal string representations of 64 characters are valid.The signing key certificate fingerprints are always obtained from the Play Store and this field is used to provide additional signing key certificate fingerprints. However, if the application is not available on the Play Store, this field needs to be set. A NonComplianceDetail with INVALID_VALUE is reported if this field is not set when the application is not available on the Play Store.The signing key certificate fingerprint of the extension app on the device must match one of the signing key certificate fingerprints obtained from the Play Store or the ones provided in this field for the app to be able to communicate with Android Device Policy.In production use cases, it is recommended to leave this empty.
---@field notificationReceiver? string Fully qualified class name of the receiver service class for Android Device Policy to notify the extension app of any local command status updates. The service must be exported in the extension app's AndroidManifest.xml and extend NotificationReceiverService (https://developers.google.com/android/management/reference/amapi/com/google/android/managementapi/notification/NotificationReceiverService) (see Integrate with the AMAPI SDK (https://developers.google.com/android/management/sdk-integration) guide for more details).

---Data hosted at an external location. The data is to be downloaded by Android Device Policy and verified against the hash.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.ExternalData
---@field url? string The absolute URL to the data, which must use either the http or https scheme. Android Device Policy doesn't provide any credentials in the GET request, so the URL must be publicly accessible. Including a long, random component in the URL may be used to prevent attackers from discovering the URL.
---@field sha256Hash? string The base-64 encoded SHA-256 hash of the content hosted at url. If the content doesn't match this hash, Android Device Policy won't use the data.

---Extra capabilities for a role.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.ExtraCapabilities
---@field localDeviceWipeCommand? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.ExtraCapabilitiesLocalDeviceWipeCommandEnum|string Optional. Controls whether the companion app can perform local device wipe (https://developers.google.com/android/management/sdk-local-commands) using AMAPI SDK (https://developers.google.com/android/management/sdk-integration).

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.ExtraCapabilitiesLocalDeviceWipeCommandEnum "LOCAL_DEVICE_WIPE_COMMAND_UNSPECIFIED"|"LOCAL_DEVICE_WIPE_COMMAND_DISALLOWED"|"LOCAL_DEVICE_WIPE_COMMAND_ALLOWED"

---A system freeze period. When a device’s clock is within the freeze period, all incoming system updates (including security patches) are blocked and won’t be installed.When the device is outside any set freeze periods, the normal policy behavior (automatic, windowed, or postponed) applies.Leap years are ignored in freeze period calculations, in particular: If Feb. 29th is set as the start or end date of a freeze period, the freeze period will start or end on Feb. 28th instead. When a device’s system clock reads Feb. 29th, it’s treated as Feb. 28th. When calculating the number of days in a freeze period or the time between two freeze periods, Feb. 29th is ignored and not counted as a day.Note: For Freeze Periods to take effect, SystemUpdateType cannot be specified as SYSTEM_UPDATE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED, because freeze periods require a defined policy to be specified.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.FreezePeriod
---@field endDate? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.Androidmanagement_Date The end date (inclusive) of the freeze period. Must be no later than 90 days from the start date. If the end date is earlier than the start date, the freeze period is considered wrapping year-end. Note: day and month must be set. year should not be set as it is not used. For example, {"month": 1,"date": 30}.
---@field startDate? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.Androidmanagement_Date The start date (inclusive) of the freeze period. Note: day and month must be set. year should not be set as it is not used. For example, {"month": 1,"date": 30}.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.FreezePeriodList gcp.androidmanagement_v1.FreezePeriod[]

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GenerateEnterpriseUpgradeUrlEnterprisesRequest
---@field allowedDomains? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.StringList Optional. A list of domains that are permitted for the admin email. The IT admin cannot enter an email address with a domain name that is not in this list. Subdomains of domains in this list are not allowed but can be allowed by adding a second entry which has *. prefixed to the domain name (e.g. *.example.com). If the field is not present or is an empty list then the IT admin is free to use any valid domain name. Personal email domains are not allowed.
---@field adminEmail? string Optional. Email address used to prefill the admin field of the enterprise signup form as part of the upgrade process. This value is a hint only and can be altered by the user. Personal email addresses are not allowed. If allowedDomains is non-empty then this must belong to one of the allowedDomains.
---@field name string Required. The name of the enterprise to be upgraded in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}.

---Response message for generating a URL to upgrade an existing managed Google Play Accounts enterprise to a managed Google domain.Note: This feature is not generally available.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GenerateEnterpriseUpgradeUrlResponse
---@field url? string A URL for an enterprise admin to upgrade their enterprise. The page can't be rendered in an iframe.

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetEnterprisesApplicationsRequest
---@field name string The name of the application in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/applications/{package_name}.
---@field languageCode? string The preferred language for localized application info, as a BCP47 tag (e.g. "en-US", "de"). If not specified the default language of the application will be used.

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetEnterprisesDevicesOperationsRequest
---@field name string The name of the operation resource.

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetEnterprisesDevicesRequest
---@field name string The name of the device in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/devices/{deviceId}.

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetEnterprisesEnrollmentTokensRequest
---@field name string Required. The name of the enrollment token in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/enrollmentTokens/{enrollmentTokenId}.

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetEnterprisesMigrationTokensRequest
---@field name string Required. The name of the migration token to retrieve. Format: enterprises/{enterprise}/migrationTokens/{migration_token}

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetEnterprisesPoliciesRequest
---@field name string The name of the policy in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/policies/{policyId}.

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetEnterprisesRequest
---@field name string The name of the enterprise in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}.

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetEnterprisesWebAppsRequest
---@field name string The name of the web app in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/webApps/{packageName}.

---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GetProvisioningInfoRequest
---@field name string Required. The identifier that Android Device Policy passes to the 3P sign-in page in the form of provisioningInfo/{provisioning_info}.

---Options for Google authentication during the enrollment.When triggering the enrollment with a SigninDetail, these options are enforced after the user completes third-party sign-in and an EnrollmentToken is created. If this token's authentication_requirement is set to REQUIRED, these options interact with the SigninDetail.googleAuthenticationOptions that initiated the flow in the following ways: - If the user skipped Google sign-in earlier (permitted by SigninDetail.googleAuthenticationOptions), an error will occur and the user will be prompted to sign in again. - If required_account_email is set on this token and the user signed in with a different email earlier, an error will occur and the user will be asked to sign in again with the correct account.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GoogleAuthenticationOptions
---@field authenticationRequirement? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GoogleAuthenticationOptionsAuthenticationRequirementEnum|string Optional. Specifies whether user should authenticate with Google during enrollment. If this is set to any value other than AUTHENTICATION_REQUIREMENT_UNSPECIFIED, the enterprise-level setting googleAuthenticationSettings is ignored for devices enrolled with this token.
---@field requiredAccountEmail? string Optional. Specifies the managed Google account that the user must use during enrollment. This field can only be set if AuthenticationRequirement is set to REQUIRED.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GoogleAuthenticationOptionsAuthenticationRequirementEnum "AUTHENTICATION_REQUIREMENT_UNSPECIFIED"|"OPTIONAL"|"REQUIRED"

---Contains settings for Google-provided user authentication.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GoogleAuthenticationSettings
---@field googleAuthenticationRequired? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GoogleAuthenticationSettingsGoogleAuthenticationRequiredEnum|string Output only. Whether users need to be authenticated by Google during the enrollment process. IT admin can specify if Google authentication is enabled for the enterprise for knowledge worker devices. This value can be set only via the Google Admin Console. Google authentication can be used with signin_url In the case where Google authentication is required and a signin_url is specified, Google authentication will be launched before signin_url. This value is overridden by EnrollmentToken.googleAuthenticationOptions and SigninDetail.googleAuthenticationOptions, if they are set.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.GoogleAuthenticationSettingsGoogleAuthenticationRequiredEnum "GOOGLE_AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED_UNSPECIFIED"|"NOT_REQUIRED"|"REQUIRED"

---Information about device hardware. The fields related to temperature thresholds are only available if hardwareStatusEnabled is true in the device's policy.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.HardwareInfo
---@field enterpriseSpecificId? string Output only. ID that uniquely identifies a personally-owned device in a particular organization. On the same physical device when enrolled with the same organization, this ID persists across setups and even factory resets. This ID is available on personally-owned devices with a work profile on devices running Android 12 and above.
---@field batteryThrottlingTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Battery throttling temperature thresholds in Celsius for each battery on the device.
---@field skinShutdownTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Device skin shutdown temperature thresholds in Celsius.
---@field cpuShutdownTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList CPU shutdown temperature thresholds in Celsius for each CPU on the device.
---@field serialNumber? string The device serial number. However, for personally-owned devices running Android 12 and above, this is the same as the enterpriseSpecificId.
---@field gpuShutdownTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList GPU shutdown temperature thresholds in Celsius for each GPU on the device.
---@field gpuThrottlingTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList GPU throttling temperature thresholds in Celsius for each GPU on the device.
---@field deviceBasebandVersion? string Baseband version. For example, MDM9625_104662.22.05.34p.
---@field hardware? string Name of the hardware. For example, Angler.
---@field cpuThrottlingTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList CPU throttling temperature thresholds in Celsius for each CPU on the device.
---@field brand? string Brand of the device. For example, Google.
---@field euiccChipInfo? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.EuiccChipInfoList Output only. Information related to the eUICC chip.
---@field manufacturer? string Manufacturer. For example, Motorola.
---@field model? string The model of the device. For example, Asus Nexus 7.
---@field batteryShutdownTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Battery shutdown temperature thresholds in Celsius for each battery on the device.
---@field skinThrottlingTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Device skin throttling temperature thresholds in Celsius.

---Hardware status. Temperatures may be compared to the temperature thresholds available in hardwareInfo to determine hardware health.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.HardwareStatus
---@field cpuUsages? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList CPU usages in percentage for each core available on the device. Usage is 0 for each unplugged core. Empty array implies that CPU usage is not supported in the system.
---@field fanSpeeds? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Fan speeds in RPM for each fan on the device. Empty array means that there are no fans or fan speed is not supported on the system.
---@field createTime? string The time the measurements were taken.
---@field gpuTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Current GPU temperatures in Celsius for each GPU on the device.
---@field skinTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Current device skin temperatures in Celsius.
---@field cpuTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Current CPU temperatures in Celsius for each CPU on the device.
---@field batteryTemperatures? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.DoubleList Current battery temperatures in Celsius for each battery on the device.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.HardwareStatusList gcp.androidmanagement_v1.HardwareStatus[]

