---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.IssueCommandEnterprisesDevicesRequest
---@field createTime? string The timestamp at which the command was created. The timestamp is automatically generated by the server.
---@field resetPasswordFlags? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.CommandResetPasswordFlagsItemEnumList For commands of type RESET_PASSWORD, optionally specifies flags.
---@field errorCode? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.CommandErrorCodeEnum|string If the command failed, an error code explaining the failure. This is not set when the command is cancelled by the caller. For reasoning about command errors, prefer fields in the following order (most preferred first): 1. Command-specific fields like clearAppsDataStatus, startLostModeStatus, or similar, if they exist. 2. This field, if set. 3. The generic error field in the Operation that wraps the command.
---@field newPassword? string For commands of type RESET_PASSWORD, optionally specifies the new password. Note: The new password must be at least 6 characters long if it is numeric in case of Android 14 devices. Else the command will fail with INVALID_VALUE.
---@field requestDeviceInfoParams? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.RequestDeviceInfoParams Optional. Parameters for the REQUEST_DEVICE_INFO command to get device related information. If this is set, then it is suggested that type should not be set. In this case, the server automatically sets it to REQUEST_DEVICE_INFO . It is also acceptable to explicitly set type to REQUEST_DEVICE_INFO.
---@field startLostModeParams? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.StartLostModeParams Parameters for the START_LOST_MODE command to put the device into lost mode. See StartLostModeParams. If this is set, then it is suggested that type should not be set. In this case, the server automatically sets it to START_LOST_MODE. It is also acceptable to explicitly set type to START_LOST_MODE.
---@field esimStatus? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.EsimCommandStatus Output only. Status of an ADD_ESIM or REMOVE_ESIM command.
---@field stopLostModeStatus? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.StopLostModeStatus Output only. Status of the STOP_LOST_MODE command to take the device out of lost mode. See StopLostModeStatus.
---@field clearAppsDataParams? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.ClearAppsDataParams Parameters for the CLEAR_APP_DATA command to clear the data of specified apps from the device. See ClearAppsDataParams. If this is set, then it is suggested that type should not be set. In this case, the server automatically sets it to CLEAR_APP_DATA. It is also acceptable to explicitly set type to CLEAR_APP_DATA.
---@field userName? string The resource name of the user that owns the device in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/users/{userId}. This is automatically generated by the server based on the device the command is sent to.
---@field requestDeviceInfoStatus? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.RequestDeviceInfoStatus Output only. Status of the REQUEST_DEVICE_INFO command.
---@field startLostModeStatus? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.StartLostModeStatus Output only. Status of the START_LOST_MODE command to put the device into lost mode. See StartLostModeStatus.
---@field wipeParams? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.WipeParams Optional. Parameters for the WIPE command to wipe the device. If this is set, then it is suggested that type should not be set. In this case, the server automatically sets it to WIPE. It is also acceptable to explicitly set type to WIPE.
---@field type? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.CommandTypeEnum|string The type of the command.
---@field removeEsimParams? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.RemoveEsimParams Optional. Parameters for the REMOVE_ESIM command to remove an eSIM profile from the device. If this is set, then it is suggested that type should not be set. In this case, the server automatically sets it to REMOVE_ESIM. It is also acceptable to explicitly set type to REMOVE_ESIM.
---@field clearAppsDataStatus? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.ClearAppsDataStatus Output only. Status of the CLEAR_APP_DATA command to clear the data of specified apps from the device. See ClearAppsDataStatus.
---@field duration? string The duration for which the command is valid. The command will expire if not executed by the device during this time. The default duration if unspecified is ten minutes. There is no maximum duration.
---@field stopLostModeParams? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.StopLostModeParams Parameters for the STOP_LOST_MODE command to take the device out of lost mode. See StopLostModeParams. If this is set, then it is suggested that type should not be set. In this case, the server automatically sets it to STOP_LOST_MODE. It is also acceptable to explicitly set type to STOP_LOST_MODE.
---@field addEsimParams? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.AddEsimParams Optional. Parameters for the ADD_ESIM command to add an eSIM profile to the device. If this is set, then it is suggested that type should not be set. In this case, the server automatically sets it to ADD_ESIM. It is also acceptable to explicitly set type to ADD_ESIM.
---@field name string The name of the device in the form enterprises/{enterpriseId}/devices/{deviceId}.

---Keyed app state reported by the app.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.KeyedAppState
---@field lastUpdateTime? string The time the app state was most recently updated.
---@field severity? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.KeyedAppStateSeverityEnum|string The severity of the app state.
