---Provides detail about non-compliance with a policy setting.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.NonComplianceDetail
---@field specificNonComplianceContext? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.SpecificNonComplianceContext Additional context for specific_non_compliance_reason.
---@field specificNonComplianceReason? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.NonComplianceDetailSpecificNonComplianceReasonEnum|string The policy-specific reason the device is not in compliance with the setting.
---@field currentValue? any If the policy setting could not be applied, the current value of the setting on the device.
---@field packageName? string The package name indicating which app is out of compliance, if applicable.
---@field settingName? string The name of the policy setting. This is the JSON field name of a top-level Policy field.
---@field fieldPath? string For settings with nested fields, if a particular nested field is out of compliance, this specifies the full path to the offending field. The path is formatted in the same way the policy JSON field would be referenced in JavaScript, that is: 1) For object-typed fields, the field name is followed by a dot then by a subfield name. 2) For array-typed fields, the field name is followed by the array index enclosed in brackets. For example, to indicate a problem with the url field in the externalData field in the 3rd application, the path would be applications[2].externalData.url
---@field installationFailureReason? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.NonComplianceDetailInstallationFailureReasonEnum|string If package_name is set and the non-compliance reason is APP_NOT_INSTALLED or APP_NOT_UPDATED, the detailed reason the app can't be installed or updated.
---@field nonComplianceReason? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.NonComplianceDetailNonComplianceReasonEnum|string The reason the device is not in compliance with the setting.

