---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PowerManagementEventList gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PowerManagementEvent[]

---A predicate is something that can be evaluated on a device at any point of time, to return true or false. This is the conjunction (logical AND) of all the individual conditions defined here. An empty Predicate always evaluates to true.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.Predicate
---@field updateAgeUpperBound? string Optional. An upper bound on the amount of time for which the update has been available. If not set or set to zero, always evaluates to true. This must be a multiple of 24 hours.
---@field timeOfDayUpperBound? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.TimeOfDay Optional. An upper bound on the current time of the day, evaluated as hh:00:00 in the device time zone. Must specify only the hour (0-23). The policy will be rejected if minutes, seconds, or nanos are set. If not set, always evaluates to true.The window closes at the specified hour (for example, a lower bound of 14 and an upper bound of 15 covers 14:00 to 15:00). When both bounds are set in the same rule, timeOfDayUpperBound must be strictly greater than timeOfDayLowerBound for the window to match; if timeOfDayUpperBound is less than or equal to timeOfDayLowerBound, the predicate evaluates to false. Setting timeOfDayUpperBound to 0 (00:00) evaluates to false for the entire day. To extend a window to the end of the day (24:00), omit timeOfDayUpperBound. To define an overnight window spanning midnight, use two rules: an evening rule with only timeOfDayLowerBound set and a morning rule with only timeOfDayUpperBound set (targeting the following day if daysOfWeek is set).
---@field dateLowerBound? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.Androidmanagement_Date Optional. A lower bound on the current date, in the device time zone. If not set, always evaluates to true.
---@field dateUpperBound? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.Androidmanagement_Date Optional. An upper bound on the current date, in the device time zone. If not set, always evaluates to true.
---@field timeOfDayLowerBound? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.TimeOfDay Optional. A lower bound on the current time of the day, evaluated as hh:00:00 in the device time zone. Must specify only the hour (0-23). The policy will be rejected if minutes, seconds, or nanos are set. If not set, always evaluates to true.
---@field daysOfWeek? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PredicateDaysOfWeekItemEnumList Optional. Evaluates to true if this list is empty or if the current day of the week in the device's local time is in this list.
---@field updateAgeLowerBound? string Optional. A lower bound on the amount of time for which the update (that is, the specific build or version) has been available to the device. This must be a multiple of 24 hours.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PredicateDaysOfWeekItemEnum "DAY_OF_WEEK_UNSPECIFIED"|"MONDAY"|"TUESDAY"|"WEDNESDAY"|"THURSDAY"|"FRIDAY"|"SATURDAY"|"SUNDAY"

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PredicateDaysOfWeekItemEnumList (gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PredicateDaysOfWeekItemEnum|string)[]

---Individual preferential network service configuration.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfig
---@field fallbackToDefaultConnection? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfigFallbackToDefaultConnectionEnum|string Optional. Whether fallback to the device-wide default network is allowed. If this is set to FALLBACK_TO_DEFAULT_CONNECTION_ALLOWED, then nonMatchingNetworks must not be set to NON_MATCHING_NETWORKS_DISALLOWED, the policy will be rejected otherwise. Note: If this is set to FALLBACK_TO_DEFAULT_CONNECTION_DISALLOWED, applications are not able to access the internet if the 5G slice is not available.
---@field preferentialNetworkId? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfigPreferentialNetworkIdEnum|string Required. Preferential network identifier. This must not be set to NO_PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK or PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_UNSPECIFIED, the policy will be rejected otherwise.
---@field nonMatchingNetworks? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfigNonMatchingNetworksEnum|string Optional. Whether apps this configuration applies to are blocked from using networks other than the preferential service. If this is set to NON_MATCHING_NETWORKS_DISALLOWED, then fallbackToDefaultConnection must be set to FALLBACK_TO_DEFAULT_CONNECTION_DISALLOWED.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfigFallbackToDefaultConnectionEnum "FALLBACK_TO_DEFAULT_CONNECTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"FALLBACK_TO_DEFAULT_CONNECTION_ALLOWED"|"FALLBACK_TO_DEFAULT_CONNECTION_DISALLOWED"

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfigList gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfig[]

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfigNonMatchingNetworksEnum "NON_MATCHING_NETWORKS_UNSPECIFIED"|"NON_MATCHING_NETWORKS_ALLOWED"|"NON_MATCHING_NETWORKS_DISALLOWED"

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfigPreferentialNetworkIdEnum "PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_ONE"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_TWO"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_THREE"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_FOUR"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_FIVE"

---Preferential network service settings.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceSettings
---@field preferentialNetworkServiceConfigs? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceConfigList Required. Preferential network service configurations which enables having multiple enterprise slices. There must not be multiple configurations with the same preferentialNetworkId. If a configuration is not referenced by any application by setting ApplicationPolicy.preferentialNetworkId or by setting defaultPreferentialNetworkId, it will be ignored. For devices on 4G networks, enterprise APN needs to be configured additionally to set up data call for preferential network service. These APNs can be added using apnPolicy.
---@field defaultPreferentialNetworkId? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceSettingsDefaultPreferentialNetworkIdEnum|string Required. Default preferential network ID for the applications that are not in applications or if ApplicationPolicy.preferentialNetworkId is set to PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_UNSPECIFIED. There must be a configuration for the specified network ID in preferentialNetworkServiceConfigs, unless this is set to NO_PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK. If set to PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_UNSPECIFIED or unset, this defaults to NO_PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK. Note: If the default preferential network is misconfigured, applications with no ApplicationPolicy.preferentialNetworkId set are not able to access the internet. This setting does not apply to the following critical apps: com.google.android.apps.work.clouddpc com.google.android.gmsApplicationPolicy.preferentialNetworkId can still be used to configure the preferential network for them.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.PreferentialNetworkServiceSettingsDefaultPreferentialNetworkIdEnum "PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_ONE"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_TWO"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_THREE"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_FOUR"|"PREFERENTIAL_NETWORK_ID_FIVE"

