---@field header? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.UserFacingMessage A short header which appears above the HTML content.

---@alias gcp.androidmanagement_v1.TermsAndConditionsList gcp.androidmanagement_v1.TermsAndConditions[]

---Represents a time of day. The date and time zone are either not significant or are specified elsewhere. An API may choose to allow leap seconds. Related types are google.type.Date and google.protobuf.Timestamp.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.TimeOfDay
---@field minutes? number Minutes of an hour. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 59.
---@field seconds? number Seconds of a minute. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 59. An API may allow the value 60 if it allows leap-seconds.
---@field hours? number Hours of a day in 24 hour format. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and typically must be less than or equal to 23. An API may choose to allow the value "24:00:00" for scenarios like business closing time.
---@field nanos? number Fractions of seconds, in nanoseconds. Must be greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to 999,999,999.

---The Unified Update Control policy, for controlling updates of software components on the device (see Target). Supported only on company-owned devices.
---@class gcp.androidmanagement_v1.UnifiedUpdatePolicy
---@field rules? gcp.androidmanagement_v1.RuleList Optional. When the policy is evaluated for a given target, all rules which refer to that target are evaluated in sequence. The first rule for which the predicate evaluates to true is considered, and its outcome is used. If no rule matches, the default update behavior applies. In other words, this behaves like a chained if-else statement.However, if an update has been available for more than a certain amount of time, any outcome of BLOCK is automatically changed to the default update behavior. At most 100 rules are allowed.

---Controls types of device activity logs collected from the device and reported via Pub/Sub notification (https://developers.google.com/android/management/notifications).
